{%- comment -%}
  Inline AU and NZ flags, so the 151 KiB country-flag sprite is never fetched.

  assets/component-country-flag.css sets one sprite as the background for every
  flag on the page. That sprite holds around 200 flags, lives on FoxEcom's own
  Shopify store rather than ORI's, and costs 151.6 KiB over the wire. This shop
  offers exactly two countries, Australia and New Zealand, so it was fetching
  all of them to draw two 20x20 icons.

  These two rules carry the flag as a data URI cropped from that sprite at 2x,
  so they cover retina at background-size: 20px 20px. A background image is
  only fetched when it actually applies to a rendered element, so once both
  flags are overridden here the sprite is never requested.

  The doubled class is deliberate. .f-country-flags.f-country-flags--AU beats
  both .f-country-flags and .f-country-flags--AU on specificity, so this works
  from the head regardless of where the sprite stylesheet is loaded.

  SAFE TO FALL BACK. Add a third country in Shopify and its flag is not here,
  so it uses the sprite rule and still renders correctly. The only cost is the
  151 KiB coming back. If that happens, re-crop from the sprite: the recipe is
  in the commit that added this file.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- style -%}
.f-country-flags.f-country-flags--AU {
  background-image: url("data:image/png;base64,");
  background-position: 0 0;
  background-size: 20px 20px;
}
.f-country-flags.f-country-flags--NZ {
  background-image: url("data:image/png;base64,");
  background-position: 0 0;
  background-size: 20px 20px;
}
{%- endstyle -%}
